{
  "_comment": "HAND-BUILT SELF-EVAL SET, NOT A BENCHMARK. Every `expect` was written from what the design says should happen BEFORE the case was run, never by recording current behaviour. Inline `text` passages are test text, not Scripture, and are never displayed as Scripture. A case with `knownFailing` still keeps its principled expectation; the field only records that the failure is known and what it reveals, so the suite stays informative without tuning the system.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "vi-psalm23-1-2-realign",
      "why": "The headline demo: re-alignment alone should all but eliminate contrary motion on a short passage.",
      "passage": {
        "fixture": "psalm-23-vi1925"
      },
      "melodies": "all",
      "baseline": "new-britain",
      "expect": {
        "baselineConflictsGt": 0,
        "improves": true,
        "winnerConflictsLte": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "vi-psalm23-1-4-cycles",
      "why": "A passage longer than the tune must cycle the phrase list, still improve, and never break a hyphenated name.",
      "passage": {
        "fixture": "psalm-23-1-4-vi1925"
      },
      "melodies": "all",
      "baseline": "new-britain",
      "expect": {
        "improves": true,
        "winnerChunksGt": 4,
        "winnerConflictsLte": 3,
        "noBreakInsideHyphenated": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "vi-john316-hu-mat-break",
      "why": "A breath must never split the compound 'hư mất' (perish). The penalty table only knows punctuation, so this is where the chunker or the model rerank must save it.",
      "passage": {
        "fixture": "john-3-16-vi1925"
      },
      "melodies": "all",
      "baseline": "new-britain",
      "expect": {
        "improves": true,
        "noBreakInside": "hư mất"
      },
      "knownFailing": "The winning setting breaks inside 'hư mất' (perish). The break-penalty table only knows punctuation, so two mid-clause breaks cost the same and the aligner picks the one that sings better. Fixes belong to the data (a word-group lexicon or a penalty for splitting a compound) or to the model's chunk-break rerank, which exists for this; the stub keeps DP order. Not tuned away."
    },
    {
      "id": "vi-baseline-already-clean",
      "why": "All-level-tone text (every syllable ngang) has no voice movement, so nothing is constrained and nothing can beat the baseline: the result set must be empty, not a relabelled baseline.",
      "passage": {
        "text": "ta đi chăn chiên trên non xanh tươi",
        "language": "vi",
        "label": "test text, not Scripture"
      },
      "melodies": [
        "new-britain"
      ],
      "baseline": "new-britain",
      "expect": {
        "baselineConflicts": 0,
        "results": 0,
        "hasFailure": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "vi-no-setting-fits",
